---
import ProseLayout from '../layouts/ProseLayout.astro';
import { site } from '../config/site';
---

<ProseLayout
  title="About"
  kicker={site.name}
  lede="An open, source-cited encyclopedia of Sanātana Dharma: its texts, their authors and commentators, the ācāryas and saints, their teachings and the traditions that carry them."
>
  <h2>What we are building</h2>
  <p>
    The aim is the most trustworthy free reference on Sanātana Dharma. Every claim carries a citation. Every
    tradition is described in its own terms, and traditional and academic views are shown side by side. Texts,
    teachers and traditions are linked to one another, so a reader can follow a commentary back to its root text,
    or an ācārya back through their gurus.
  </p>

  <h2>Who it is for</h2>
  <p>
    Seekers and curious readers, students, practitioners exploring traditions beyond their own, and researchers who
    need a reliable starting point. Entries are written for an educated general reader, and technical terms are
    glossed when they first appear.
  </p>

  <h2>What makes it different</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Relational.</strong> A text links to its authors, its commentaries and the traditions that hold it
      authoritative. A teacher links to gurus, disciples, works and institutions. These links are computed from the
      data, so they stay consistent.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Two views, labelled.</strong> Where the traditional account and academic scholarship differ, as they
      often do on dates and authorship, both are given, each with its source.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Primary text first.</strong> Text entries point to the original text and to openly licensed
      translations.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Transparent.</strong> Every page shows how it was written and how far it has been verified. See
      <a href="/how-this-is-written/">how this is written</a>.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Status</h2>
  <p>
    The encyclopedia is under construction. The first entries are in place, and new ones are added through reviewed
    pull requests. The <a href={`${site.repo.url}/blob/main/MASTER_PROMPT.md`}>project plan</a> describes the phases
    ahead, including a verse-by-verse reader for the primary texts and a Hindi edition.
  </p>

  <h2>Open source</h2>
  <p>
    Everything is developed in the open on <a href={site.repo.url}>GitHub</a>. Original text and data are licensed
    under <a href={site.license.url} rel="license">{site.license.name}</a>, and the code under the MIT licence.
    Quoted material keeps its own licence, which is recorded alongside it. Corrections, suggestions and expert
    reviewers are welcome: see <a href="/contribute/">how to contribute</a>.
  </p>
</ProseLayout>
